cargo-zempic 0.0.1
    workspace: [WORKSPACE_ROOT]  (1 members, 1 selected)
      profile: release  (inherits: none)
optimizing for: size
       target: aarch64-apple-darwin

TIER 2  COMPILER                                                      2 findings

  HIGH   large  profile/opt-level:size           3 -> "z"
        effort: trivial   runtime cost: notable   fix: consequential
        The compiler optimizes for speed. Optimizing for size lets it drop code
        that exists only to run faster.
        Tradeoff: Runtime cost, pronounced with `"z"` on compute-heavy code.
  MEDIUM moderate profile/dependency-opt-level     unset -> "z"
        effort: trivial   runtime cost: none   fix: safe
        The profile's optimization level applies to dependencies too. A glob
        override optimizes them for size while leaving the workspace's members
        on the profile's setting.
        Tradeoff: The override applies to dependencies, not to workspace members.
SUMMARY
  2 findings: 1 high, 1 medium.  By magnitude: 1 large, 1 moderate.
  2 auto-fixable.

  Magnitude is an ordinal judgement, not a measurement. zempic does not build
  and does not read compiled artifacts, so it reports no sizes.
